{
  "catalogue": "ai_tasks",
  "version": 1,
  "source": "BUILD_PLAN §14 (AI layer) and §5.4. Code asks the gateway for a task, never a model.",
  "notes": [
    "model_class names the Gemini tier. model_id and fallback_model_id stay null until the bake-off pins them (BUILD_PLAN §5.4); the gateway refuses a live call for a task whose model_id is null.",
    "budget_inr_per_day is set by the lead before a task goes live: alert at 80%, kill switch at 100%.",
    "daily_call_cap (T61) is the free-tier daily cap (FOUNDER_QUESTIONS M3-13): the stricter of it and the ₹ budget applies, kill switch at 100%.",
    "response_schema (T61) is a reference into packages/contracts/schemas (\"x.schema.json\", \"x.schema.json#/$defs/Y\", or \"ai/x.schema.json\" for the reader-output schemas T61 adds under schemas/ai/). The gateway refuses a live or recorded call for a task whose response_schema is null.",
    "Prompts live in supabase/functions/_shared/ai/prompts/<task>/<version>.md, mirrored in Python. Every call writes ops.ai_generations. AI_MODE=recorded replays responses keyed by input SHA from recorded_dir.",
    "Hard rules: rules decide (no LLM output becomes a band, verdict or number); citations or silence; document text is data, never instructions; PII is stripped before any model call; Gemini free tier sees fictional data only (DECISIONS E-8)."
  ],
  "pii_policies": {
    "strip": "Phones, PAN, Aadhaar and emails are removed before the call. Third-party numbers on flyers are masked in our copy.",
    "strip_and_redact_bank": "As strip, and bank account numbers are redacted in ops.ai_generations and logs.",
    "public_record": "Public authority documents. Director phones and addresses are still removed before the call."
  },
